[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit Accepted"]
[Variation "Fischer Defence, 4.Bc4"]
[ECO "C34"]
[Character "solid,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "extra-pawn,kingside-space"]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 d6 4. Bc4 4... h6 { Stops a knight or bishop from landing on g5, where it would aim at f7. The pawn also makes ...g5 possible. }
5. d4 5... g5 { Holds the f4 pawn. Without it White would recapture on f4 and have a free centre. }
6. h4 6... Bg7 { Develops the bishop on the long diagonal, where it pressures d4, and makes room to castle. }
7. Nc3 7... Nc6 { Hits the pawn on d4, so White has to keep defending it. [%cal Gc6d4] }
8. Qd3 8... Bg4 { Attacks the knight on f3, which is guarding d4, so White's centre comes under more pressure. }
9. Bb5 (9. hxg5 hxg5 10. Rxh8+ Bxh8 11. Ne2 Qf6)
9... Bd7 { Blocks the pin on the knight on c6 by putting the bishop on d7. } 10. Bxc6 bxc6 11. Bd2 g4 { Attacks the knight on f3, which holds White's centre together. } *
